/*
  KG-QL: Benchmark Agent

  JaCaMo project file for the Gradle task "taskBench".

  Starts one BDI agent, illuminance_controller_agent_bench
  (src/agt/illuminance_controller_agent_bench.asl). It runs the benchmark
  scenarios of the selected lab profile with one control mode and writes one
  result file, benchmark_results_<mode>.csv.

  To run: ./gradlew taskBench -Pmode=<mode>
          (while the Node-RED simulator flow of that profile is running; the
          port of each lab is the sim_port in src/agt/lab_profiles.asl)

  Options:
    -Pmode=rule_based | ql_false | ql_true
        rule_based  fixed hand-written control rules, no learning
        ql_false    greedy policy from the Q-table trained without knowledge
        ql_true     greedy policy from the Q-table trained with the knowledge graph
        The value is passed as the system property bench.mode and replaces the
        default of the bench_mode belief in the agent program.
    The lab profile is the active_profile belief of the agent program; the
    run_full_project.ps1 script sets it for each lab. The agent also reads the
    system property active.profile, which the Gradle task does not set.

  For ql_false and ql_true the Q-table files written by the training run
  (task_ql.jcm) must exist, e.g. qtable_final_stereotypes_true.csv and
  qtable_final_stereotypes_false.csv. Run once per mode.
*/

mas lab_bench {

    agent illuminance_controller_agent_bench

}
